course: dictionary
lesson: 4537
title: An old word: hearken
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound old because they are old. Hearken is one of them. It means to listen carefully, and you will meet it in old stories, songs and the Bible. «Hearken unto me» is an old way of saying "Listen to me."
explain: Read the clues around the word. In «Hearken unto me», the speaker is calling for attention, so hearken must be about listening. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Listen unto me" still makes sense, so you have the right idea. Old words often sound grand and formal, like a storyteller asking for quiet.
explain: Hearken has a second meaning, hearken back to. To hearken back to something is to go back to it or remind people of something from the past. If a new phone's design hearkens back to an old radio, the design is reminding you of the past. Today people often say hark back instead.
fact: Hearken means to listen carefully.
fact: «Hearken» is an old-fashioned word, found in old stories, songs and the Bible.
fact: «Hearken unto me» means "Listen to me."
fact: Hearken back to means to go back to something or remind people of the past.
fact: Hearken can also be spelled harken.
exercise: What does «hearken» mean in «Hearken unto me»? | Shout loudly | Fall fast asleep | *Listen carefully | Run away quickly
exercise: Kipling's storytellers write, «Hear and attend and listen». Which word means the same as hearken? | Wander | Shout | Sleep | *Attend
exercise: Ben says, "That new song hearkens back to the 1980s." What does hearkens back to mean? | *Goes back to, or reminds us of, the past | Is played very loudly | Forgets the 1980s completely | Comes from the future
test: Why is hearken an old word? | It is brand new slang from social media | *It is old-fashioned and used in stories, songs and the Bible | It is the name of a country | It is a word that only means shouting
test: What does hearken back to mean? | *Go back to something, or remind people of the past | Forget something completely | Shout at someone from far away | Build something very quickly
exam: Which spelling is another correct way to write hearken? | Herken | Heark | *Harken | Hearkon
